# tree-arb: the join levels read two slices each (fan-in 2), with staged,
# shared and zero-latency links around them.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/tree-arb
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/tz --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --compact-links --staged-links --share-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --class-at 'sl@*.slice' --class-at 'root@inner:arb' --csf-single-bank --csf-mailbox-builder 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TZ
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/tz/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/tz/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/tz/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/tz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +stall=0 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/tz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +stall=60 | FileCheck %s
# `--csf-mailbox-hbm`: the mailboxes in HBM, a stream of reader rows each
# (Src -> Sink: two Sink rows of four lanes, a reader-indexed mailbox; Sink ->
# Src, where each Src reads one Sink row: a producer-indexed stream sliced by
# reader (four pages, a Src group's ready bit each), its
# readiness lanes fanning out), written byte-masked at the producer's pass, a row landing for
# each reader pass in the stream's landing slots, two sets of read registers
# in turn (no spacing of the reader's passes). Against the controllers'
# model (Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv: 1 to 60 host cycles, stalls, full, the
# protocol checked), frames of 40 and 24 (min-ii) with bubbles, and with the
# on-chip builder, shared and staged links beside.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/mailbox
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/h40 --static --nest --modulo --min-ii 40 --compact-links --csf-mailbox-hbm --bubbles Src Sink 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HBM
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HBMS < %t/h40/schedule.txt
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HBMVH < %t/h40/foldsim_sim.vh
# Each stream's landings-in-flight count (a table of the position) is read
# through a lookahead register loaded a host cycle before, like the virtual
# memories' tables: not decoded from the position in the advance's cone.
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HBMAHEAD < %t/h40/foldsim_sim.mlir
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/h40 -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/h40/obj %S/Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv top.sv %t/h40/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/h40/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/h40/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h40/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 +bubble=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h40/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# A fixed HBM latency below the streams' leads (25 and 33 at II 40, less the
# decision lead and a landing's margin) is hidden: H is the frame's (II 40),
# at latency 1 as at 18 (the landings decided and not yet run alone are
# waited for, not the next ones of a sparse stream).
# RUN: %t/h40/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=1 +hi=1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HII
# RUN: %t/h40/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=18 +hi=18 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HII
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/h24 --static --nest --modulo --min-ii 24 --compact-links --share-links --staged-links --csf-single-bank --csf-mailbox-builder --csf-mailbox-hbm --bubbles Src Sink > %t/h24.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=H24 < %t/h24/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/h24 -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/h24/obj %S/Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv top.sv %t/h24/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/h24/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/h24/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h24/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+6 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 +bubble=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/h24/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# A stream member that carries some reader instances alone (the others at
# the frame's wrap read an on-chip link of their own rows), one of whose
# on-chip rests takes the producer's write in its slot or forwards it past
# the read register (its hits masked to its own instances): linkhbm's
# Unit/Reader with csf-mailbox-hbm, exact with latencies 1 to 80, stalls and
# bubbles. (The masks are by construction: no false hit arises here, and
# none in the synthetic designs tried.)
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/linkhbm
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/pm --static --nest --modulo --compact-links --share-links --staged-links --zero-latency-links --zero-latency-chains --bubbles --csf-mailbox-hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PM
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/pm -DVM1 -DVM2 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/pm/obj %S/Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv top.sv %t/pm/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/pm/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/pm/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/pm/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 +bubble=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/pm/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +lo=5 +hi=80 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# PM: hbm 3 (3 of some reader instances, 1 with the rest's takes or forwards masked)
# Rows of 8 bits (--csf-mailbox-hbm-row-bits 8): a mailbox lane of 32 bits
# wider than a row (Unit -> Reader) would take four landings a reader pass
# and space the reader's passes, so it stays on chip (one landing a pass:
# only its 8-bit lane streams); a producer word of 32 bits wider than a row
# whose reader takes it whole (Reader -> Unit) is a stream of 32-bit rows (as
# layoutStreamsOf lays it out); exact.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/rb8 --static --nest --modulo --min-ii 48 --compact-links --share-links --staged-links --bubbles --csf-mailbox-hbm --csf-mailbox-hbm-row-bits 8 Unit Reader > %t/rb8.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RB8 < %t/rb8/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/rb8 -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/rb8/obj %S/Inputs/tb_mailbox_hbm.sv top.sv %t/rb8/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/rb8/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/rb8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/rb8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 +bubble=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/rb8/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +lo=5 +hi=80 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RB8: link streams: 2 streams, 2 links
# RB8: link stream Reader Unit 1 0 32 32 1
# RB8-NOT: link stream Unit Reader 1 0 32
# RB8: link stream Unit Reader 1 0 8 8 1
# HBM: II = 40
# HII: MATCH 196 cycles in 7966 host cycles, H 39.83
# HBMS: link streams: 2 streams, 12 links, 80 bits
# HBMS: link stream Sink Src 4 0 32 8 4 8 8 1
# HBMS: link stream Src Sink 8 0 32 32 1 8 2 1
# H24: link streams: 2 streams, 11 links, 76 bits
# H24: link stream Sink Src 3 1 32 8 4 8 6 1
# H24: link stream Src Sink 8 0 32 32 1 8 2 1
# The window's slots' pending bits, registers (a select of the slot entering
# it, not one a slot).
# HBMAHEAD-DAG: %lks{{[0-9]+}}_ahead0 = seq.firreg {{%[^ ]+}} clock %hostClock reset sync %hostReset, {{%[^ ]+}} preset 0 : i1
# The landings-in-flight count is read through lookahead registers (one-bit
# landing tables summed, as the PP landing windows do), not decoded at `next`.
# HBMAHEAD: %vready_ahead{{[0-9]+}} = seq.firreg {{%[^ ]+}} clock %hostClock reset sync %hostReset, {{%[^ ]+}} preset {{[0-9]+}} : i1
# A stream's landing table at `next` - d (d < the window): one lookahead table,
# the others its registers shifted as `next` steps (no table each).
# HBMAHEAD-DAG: %landed_ahead{{[0-9]+}} = seq.firreg {{%[^ ]+}} clock %hostClock reset sync %hostReset, {{%[^ ]+}} preset {{[0-9]+}} : i1
# HBMVH: FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_DW 8
# HBMVH-NEXT: FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_MW 1
# HBMVH: FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_DW 32
# HBMVH-NEXT: FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_MW 4
# PLAIN: csf mailboxes: 2 (1 two banks) of 2 plans, 11 links as lanes (416 producer-entry bits), 2 memories (2 masked), 224 bits
# CP: csf mailboxes: 4 (2 two banks) of 4 plans, 22 links as lanes (416 producer-entry bits), 4 memories (4 masked), 320 bits
# ZL: csf mailboxes: 2 (1 two banks) of 2 plans, 10 links as lanes (320 producer-entry bits), 2 memories (2 masked), 192 bits
# TZ: csf mailboxes: 1 (1 two banks) of 1 plans, 4 links as lanes (108 producer-entry bits), 1 memories (1 masked), 128 bits
# A mailbox: a reader row per Sink, written with a byte mask.
# PLAINSIM: %Src_to_Sink_mbox0_0 = seq.firmem 0, 1, undefined, undefined : <4 x 32, mask 4>
# BLKSIM: %Src_to_Sink_mbox0_0 = seq.firmem 1, 1, old, undefined {{.*}}block{{.*}} : <4 x 32, mask 4>
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH
# CHECK-NOT: MISMATCH
